WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:06.840
For fans of schlocky horror, 2023 is off to&nbsp;
a sweet start. After months of viral hype,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:10.380
"Winnie-the-Pooh: Blood and Honey" is&nbsp;
almost here. Here's all you need to know.

00:00:10.380 --> 00:00:16.080
For horror aficionados, Winter 2023 is&nbsp;
all about the viral dancing robot slasher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:21.180
"M3GAN," M. Night Shyamalan's "Knock at the&nbsp;
Cabin," "Scream 6," and, for the real sickos,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:25.620
the childhood-tarnishing "Winnie-the-Pooh:&nbsp;
Blood and Honey." Such a project is possible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:30.960
thanks to the original "Winnie-the-Pooh" IP&nbsp;
entering the public domain in January of 2022.

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:35.280
The first trailer for "Winnie-the-Pooh:&nbsp;
Blood and Honey" premiered in August of 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.280 --> 00:00:39.000
providing viewers with their first look&nbsp;
at its murderous versions of Pooh and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.020
Piglet in action since still images of&nbsp;
the characters first appeared in May.

00:00:43.247 --> 00:00:46.787
"We used to be friends. Why are you doing this?"

00:00:46.787 --> 00:00:51.780
The trailer opens with an adult Christopher&nbsp;
Robin introducing his fiancee Mary to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.780 --> 00:00:56.640
Hundred Acre Wood, where he spent his childhood&nbsp;
taking care of Pooh and company. Christopher,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.620
however, has trouble locating his old friends,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:02.700
and even stumbles upon a makeshift&nbsp;
scrap lumber gravestone for Eeyore.

00:01:03.420 --> 00:01:04.680
"Thank you, Pooh."

00:01:06.272 --> 00:01:10.560
Pooh seemingly dispatches Christopher and&nbsp;
Mary with ease, before directing his and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:14.340
Piglet's murder spree toward a group of&nbsp;
college girls staying at a rural cabin,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:19.560
where the balance of the film looks to take place.&nbsp;
Naturally, the trailer concludes with glimpses of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.560 --> 00:01:24.300
horrified and sometimes bloody faces, teasing the&nbsp;
kills that will likely drive "Blood and Honey."

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:30.540
In June of 2022, shortly after its core concept&nbsp;
went viral online, Dread Central spoke with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:34.740
director of "Winnie-the-Pooh: Blood and Honey,"&nbsp;
Rhys Frake-Waterfield, about the film's plot.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:38.760
Notably, he made it clear that Pooh&nbsp;
and Piglet are not humans in masks,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:44.460
but instead a humanoid bear and a humanoid pig,&nbsp;
just as in the source text. Their reason for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.460 --> 00:01:47.520
becoming violent is that Christopher&nbsp;
Robin fed them when he was younger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:51.600
before growing up and leaving them to fend&nbsp;
for themselves without a proper source of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:56.520
food. They hunt and kill humans, then, both for&nbsp;
sustenance and out of anger at their lot in life.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:59.100
The general public first&nbsp;
learned of "Winnie-the-Pooh:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.100 --> 00:02:03.720
Blood and Honey" around May of 2022, at&nbsp;
which point filming had already wrapped,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:08.280
according to an early profile that Variety&nbsp;
published around that time. The "Blood and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.280 --> 00:02:11.760
Honey" team, it turns out, was able&nbsp;
to conclude filming in just 10 days.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:17.100
Fittingly, the project was filmed near the Ashdown&nbsp;
Forest located on the outskirts of East Sussex,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:21.480
England, which once served as inspiration for the&nbsp;
Hundred Acre Wood in which "Winnie-the-Pooh" takes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:26.100
place. Then, after receiving positive responses&nbsp;
to early still photos of "Blood and Honey,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:30.780
its creators decided to expedite its release to&nbsp;
make the most of the growing momentum behind it.

00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:33.360
As a result of this quick&nbsp;
turnaround, "Winnie-the-Pooh:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:38.220
Blood and Honey" will hit theaters in&nbsp;
the United States on February 15, 2023,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.220 --> 00:02:43.740
as a single-day theatrical engagement, so those&nbsp;
interested in catching it in theaters will have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:48.120
to plan to see it that very day. "Blood and&nbsp;
Honey" will also screen in the United Kingdom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.120 --> 00:02:52.740
Canada, Mexico, and some additional&nbsp;
countries, though whether or not it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:56.820
will remain in theaters for a longer period&nbsp;
of time worldwide has yet to be announced.

00:02:56.820 --> 00:02:59.700
"Blood and Honey" is a decidedly&nbsp;
independent production,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:04.470
so its cast is largely composed not of&nbsp;
marquee names, but instead of actors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.470 --> 00:03:07.980
whose experience consists predominantly&nbsp;
of other independent horror projects.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:11.580
Director Rhys Frake-Waterfield has&nbsp;
served as a producer on more than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:16.920
20 such independent horror movies, most of&nbsp;
which were released between 2021 and 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.920 --> 00:03:22.320
and draw from similarly over-the-top premises.&nbsp;
These include films with names like "Dinosaur&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:27.960
Hotel," "The Legend of Jack and Jill," "Kingdom&nbsp;
of the Dinosaurs," and "Curse of Jack Frost."

00:03:27.960 --> 00:03:33.540
As a director, Frake-Waterfield's past work&nbsp;
consists of three releases: a short titled&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:39.180
"Go Viral," alien horror film "The Area 51&nbsp;
Incident," and the cheeky Christmas slasher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.180 --> 00:03:43.140
"Demonic Christmas Tree." Furthermore,&nbsp;
Frake-Waterfield's name is attached to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:48.780
several upcoming releases beyond just "Blood and&nbsp;
Honey," including "Dinosaur Prison," "Firenado,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.780 --> 00:03:53.868
and "Rise of Loch Ness," all of which seem&nbsp;
to indicate their premises in their titles.

